%%{init:{'theme':'base'}}%%
%% Scene Builder: Layered Rendering Flowchart
%% Shows modular room upgrades via prioritized layers and decoration lookup.
flowchart TD
  Start([Start: render room scene]) --> FetchDeco{Fetch room decorations}

  FetchDeco --> QueryDB[Query user_room_decoration table for all layers]

  subgraph RoomLayers [Room Layer Loop]
    direction TB
    QueryDB --> CheckLayer{Decoration exists for layer?}
    CheckLayer -->|Yes| UseUserImg[Use user decoration image pointer]
    CheckLayer -->|No| UseDefault[Use default/fallback image]
    UseUserImg --> Stack[Add image to layer stack at its priority]
    UseDefault --> Stack
    Stack --> MoreLayers{More layers remaining?}
    MoreLayers -->|Yes| CheckLayer
    MoreLayers -->|No| LayersDone[Room layers completed]
  end

  LayersDone --> PlantFlow{Render plants and pots}

  subgraph PlantLayers [Plant Layer Loop]
    direction TB
    PlantFlow --> CheckPlantDeco{Check user_room_decoration for plant/pot overlays}
    CheckPlantDeco -->|Exists| UsePlantUser[Use user image pointer for pot/overlay]
    CheckPlantDeco -->|Missing| UsePlantDefault[Use default pot/plant asset]
    UsePlantUser --> ComposePlant[Compose plant layers in priority order]
    UsePlantDefault --> ComposePlant
    ComposePlant --> PlantDone[Plant layers composed]
  end

  PlantDone --> ComposeScene[Compose room and plant layer stacks into final scene]
  ComposeScene --> Render[Render final composed scene to canvas/DOM]
  Render --> End([End])

  %% Notes
  classDef note fill:#f9f9f9,stroke:#333,stroke-width:0.5;
  Note1([Modular layering allows swapping backgrounds, walls, windows, windowsills, weather, curtains])
  Note2([Plant layering uses fewer layers and simpler rules])
  Note3([Decoration lookup: if user_room_decoration has an entry for a layer, use its image pointer; otherwise use a default asset])

  class Note1 note
  class Note2 note
  class Note3 note

  Start -.-> Note1
  Start -.-> Note2
  QueryDB -.-> Note3
